# Local artifact root. Retention convention established 2026-09-27:
#   _out/evidence/<name>/   durable evidence a tracked doc or a Basic Memory note points at
#   _out/preserved-*/       keepers moved out of a scratch tree rather than deleted
#   _out/perf-runs/         per-run perf/benchmark output -- SEED STATE AND RAW DUMPS ARE
#                           REGENERABLE, reports are not. A retention pass on 2026-09-27 removed
#                           8,504.8 MB (79%) of per-run baluffo-runtime.db copies, their -wal/-shm
#                           sidecars, replicated seed-data/jobs-fetch-report.json, and raw
#                           measurement dumps, while preserving all 7 cited run directories whole.
#                           Deleted paths are recorded in
#                           _out/perf-runs-retention-20260927/deleted-manifest.json.
#                           Rule: keep every .md and every cited path. The .db files are each run's
#                           end state (their hashes differ), so deleting them discards results
#                           rather than duplicates -- which is why the cited runs were kept whole.
#   Never purge _out/ by name or age. Decide by reference, and write a manifest of what went.
_out/
.state/
.cursor/
.vscode/debug-brave-profile/
coverage-report/

# Build/runtime artifact cleanup
tmp-manual-check/
tmp-pytest-bridge/
# Repo-root agent scratch (never tracked; the documented artifact root is .tmp/).
# Unignored it is ~3k files / 740 MB of logs, JSON dumps, and registry backups,
# which trips check-added-large-files for any `git add -A` submit.
#
# Convention, established 2026-09-27: do NOT cite a path under /tmp/ from a tracked doc, and do
# not put durable evidence there. 47 of the 87 directories in tmp/ turned out to be provenance
# cited by docs/CHANGELOG.md and the plan/snapshot docs; all 47 now live in _out/evidence/<name>/
# with every citation rewritten. tmp/ reads as scratch and is the first thing anyone purges, so
# anything a shipped change points at belongs in _out/ (ignored, so local-only either way -- the
# move changes intent, not durability).
#
# /tmp/ is NOT all disposable. These are operational runtime paths the application itself
# resolves, and rewriting them to another root breaks the app. They are excluded from the
# evidence relocation on purpose:
#   tmp/baluffo-ship            desktop runtime data root
#   tmp/desktop.lock            desktop single-instance lock
#   tmp/pytest                  pytest temp root
#   tmp/packaged-desktop-smoke  packaged smoke output (and -pair)
#   tmp/availability-preflight-diagnostics.json   written by src code on a failed run
/tmp/
release-notes.md
.container-frontend/

# Local runtime/generated data (keep local, do not track)
data/*.json
data/*.csv
data/*.log
data/*.md
data/*.jsonl
data/*.jsonl.gz
# Rotation siblings (e.g. storage-metrics.jsonl.1) are not matched by *.jsonl
data/*.jsonl.*
data/*.lock
data/*.db
data/*.db-*
data/*.json.gz
